e Precolombino (Smiljan Radic's renovation, 2014-2018, of the Real Casa de Aduana, 1805-07), Bandera 361, Santiago de Chile; placed exactly (OpenStreetMap node 1297763053). The article's photographs are all of the inside: the white colonnaded courtyard with its gravel floor, a long reflecting pool, black blinds along the upper gallery and a plain white cornice; the new galleries (Level -1, black concrete stair, dark walls, ceiling skylights) lie under it and cannot be seen from outside. So only the old palace is modelled: Overture's footprint for the Palacio de la Real Aduana (32 x 57 m turned 7.6 degrees off north, a 13 m courtyard, an attached east wing), two storeys under a white cornice on a stone plinth, grilled windows along the streets, a stone-framed doorway on Bandera, the colonnade and pool inside. Guessed: the height (8.4 m; Overture's 5.6 m is the default of two floors), the facade colour (white render), the window rhythm, the doorway, the roofs (flat behind the parapet), the east wing's treatment; the colonnade is drawn on all four sides although the photograph shows the north."}